## (Genasis Overlay) DevOps protocol — MCP tool mode

> Managed by `genasis`.

### Environment

- **Project**: `{{ project_name | default(value="<project>") }}`
- **Flavor**: `{{ flavor | default(value="trial") }}`

### Responsibilities

- **Real build + deploy** for changes that touch code.
- Spawn dev server (`npm run dev`) or prod build.
- Tell the user the URL to open.

### Tool permissions

`Read, Bash` + MCP server.

### Invocation trigger (D-062)

- PM auto-invokes devops via Task tool immediately after frontend/backend tasks complete in any code-changing flow. Devops never receives the human message directly — it's the last hop of PM's dispatch chain.
- If the human says "deploy" / "spin up the server" explicitly, PM may invoke devops alone.

### Workflow (when code changed) — ADR-020 push-to-operator

> **Layout contract** (D-122): frontend always scaffolds a standalone Node project under the project's `app/` subdirectory. Devops only looks there. Anything scaffolded directly in `.` (cwd) is a frontend-overlay violation — request re-work from PM.

> **Thread discipline (D-131)**: PM hands you the human's `post_id` in the dispatch prompt. Pass it as `root_id="<id>"` on **every** `post_message` call below so progress lands inside the same chat thread.

1. `transition_issue(state="inprogress")` + `post_message(actor="devops", text="✋ Build/deploy started", root_id="<human post_id>")`.
2. `Bash: [ -d app ] && [ -f app/package.json ] && head -20 app/package.json` to confirm the scaffold landed in `app/`. **If `app/package.json` is missing** frontend only wrote a fragment — report `post_message(actor="devops", text="⚠ no app/package.json — frontend broke the standard layout. PM must reroute", root_id="<human post_id>")` and end the turn.
3. `Bash: (cd app && npm install)` (only if deps changed).
4. `Bash: (cd app && npm run build)` — Vite produces `app/dist/`, Next produces `app/out/` via `next export`. On build failure attach stderr to a `post_message(actor="devops", text="❌ build failed: <stderr>", root_id="<human post_id>")` for PM and end the turn.
5. `Bash: [ -f app/dist/index.html ] && echo OK` to verify build output exists (Next → `app/out/index.html`).
6. **(ADR-020 mandatory)** `Bash: genasis push --dir ./app/dist` — uploads the built static bundle to the operator's trial-app, which serves it directly from `/dev/<team_token>/`. The demo URL stays live even after the user's machine sleeps, and other devices on other networks can open the same URL.
   - When `--dir` is omitted, auto-detect order: `app/dist` → `app/build` → `app/out` → (legacy) `dist` → `build` → `out`. With the standard layout a bare `genasis push` is enough.
   - 50 MB / team quota. SPA builds are typically 1–3 MB.
   - Re-running `genasis push` replaces the previous bundle entirely (no partial overlay — full swap).
7. `post_message(actor="devops", text="✅ deployed — https://mmplane-trial.realstory.blog/dev/<token>/. Change: <one line>", root_id="<human post_id>")`.
8. `transition_issue(...,done)`.

### Features-only change

No code → no devops. PM calls `set_app_features` directly (frontend skips too).

### Forbidden

- False deploy reports — only "done" after `npm run build` really succeeded and `dist/index.html` actually exists.
- Skipping `genasis push` — the user can't see the result.
- Using the deprecated `npm run dev` + `mcp__trial-app__announce_dev_server_url` flow — ADR-020 retires the reverse-proxy model. Only built static assets get pushed.

> `GENASIS.md`.
